nia Tech, to face Wake Forest in ACC title game","description":"Miami will play Wake Forest in the ACC title game on Dec. 5 after both teams won on Saturday.","published":"2026-11-22T04:46:52.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50558418/miami-tops-virginia-tech-face-wake-forest-acc-title-game","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Betting buzz: Big Ten's odds of national champion four-peat getting slim","description":"Losses by UCLA, Indiana and Ohio State make the Big Ten's chances of winning the national championship this season a long shot.","published":"2026-11-22T04:06:20.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/49921234/college-football-betting-buzz-odds-updates-line-moves-spreads","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Emotional Greg Schiano authors 'special' win, Rutgers' first at PSU since 1988","description":"Less than two weeks after Rutgers announced embattled Greg Schiano would return as coach for a 19th season, the Scarlet Knights stunned Penn State 25-24 on Saturday, their first win over the Nittany Lions since 1988, and just their third this year.","published":"2026-11-22T02:56:26.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50557643/rutgers-authors-special-win-1st-penn-state-1988","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4922988/jamari-johnson","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jamari_Johnson"},"pick":{"pick":22,"round":1,"team":"NYG","provisional":true},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Jamari Johnson","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jamari_Johnson","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-22T04:18:12Z","intro":"Jamari Johnson is an American college football tight end for the Oregon Ducks. He previously played for the Louisville Cardinals.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Johnson attended Inglewood High School in Inglewood, California. He originally played quarterback before switching to tight end and also played wide receiver, running back and defensive end. As a senior, he was named the Ocean League MVP. Johnson was selected to play in the 2023 All-American Bowl. He committed to the University of Louisville to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Johnson played in five games and redshirted his first year at Louisville in 2023. He played in seven games as a redshirt freshman in 2024, recording 13 receptions for 158 yards and a touchdown, before suffering a season ending ankle injury. After the season, he entered the transfer portal and transferred to the University of Oregon. Johnson spent his first season at Oregon in 2025 as the backup to Kenyon Sadiq."}]}}